   "source": [
    "# Working with parquet files\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "+ In this assignment, we will use the data downloaded with the module `data_manager` to create features.\n",
    "\n",
    "(11 pts total)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "+ This notebook assumes that price data is available to you in the environment variable `PRICE_DATA`. If you have not done so, then execute the notebook `production_2_data_engineering.ipynb` to create this data set.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "+ Load the environment variables using dotenv. (1 pt)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Write your code below.\n",
    "%load_ext dotenv\n",
    "%dotenv \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import dask\n",
    "dask.config.set({'dataframe.query-planning': True})\n",
    "import dask.dataframe as dd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "+ Load the environment variable `PRICE_DATA`.\n",
    "+ Use [glob](https://docs.python.org/3/library/glob.html) to find the path of all parquet files in the directory `PRICE_DATA`.\n",
    "\n",
    "(1pt)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'../../05_src/data/prices/'"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os \n",
    "os.getenv('PRICE_DATA')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "../../05_src/data/prices/\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os \n",
    "from glob import glob \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Write your code below.\n",
    "PRICE_DATA = os.getenv('PRICE_DATA')\n",
    "print(PRICE_DATA)\n",
    "parquet_files = glob(os.path.join(PRICE_DATA, \"*/**/*.parquet\"))\n",
    "dd_px = dd.read_parquet(parquet_files).set_index(\"ticker\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For each ticker and using Dask, do the following:\n",
    "\n",
    "+ Add lags for variables Close and Adj_Close.\n",
    "+ Add returns based on Adjusted Close:\n",
    "    \n",
    "    - `returns`: (Adj Close / Adj Close_lag) - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "+ Add the following range: \n",
    "\n",
    "    - `hi_lo_range`: this is the day's High minus Low.\n",
    "\n",
    "+ Assign the result to `dd_feat`.\n",
    "\n",
    "(4 pt)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Function to add lags\n",
    "def add_lags(df):\n",
    "    df['Close_lag_1'] = df['Close'].shift(1)\n",
    "    return df\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Empty DataFrame\n",
      "Columns: [Date, Open, High, Low, Close, Adj Close, Volume, sector, subsector, year]\n",
      "Index: []\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Write your code below.\n",
    "import dask.dataframe as dd\n",
    "\n",
    "def add_lags(df):\n",
    "    df['Close_lag'] = df['Close'].shift(1)\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Function to compute returns based on 'Close'\n",
    "def compute_returns(df):\n",
    "    df['returns'] = (df['Close'] / df['Close_lag']) - 1\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Function to calculate high-low range\n",
    "def compute_hi_lo_range(df):\n",
    "    df['hi_lo_range'] = df['High'] - df['Low']\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "dd_feat = dd_px.groupby('ticker').apply(add_lags, meta=dd_px).\\\n",
    "                  groupby('ticker').apply(compute_returns, meta=dd_px).\\\n",
    "                  groupby('ticker').apply(compute_hi_lo_range, meta=dd_px)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(dd_feat.head())\n"
   ]
  },
